findings.description:
The design adds three drift conditions:
- a `nodeIds` entry that resolves to a function or class;
- a `nodeIds` entry that resolves to nothing (the walkthrough jq at line 353 emits `UNRESOLVED`, but the prose never names this case);
- a surviving node with no `filePath`.

For each, it only says "reported as such". It does not say:
- where the report goes (console, the provenance Flagged-gaps line, or a body marker);
- whether the run stops or continues;
- whether the drifting node counts toward the layer total and toward the 238 reconciliation.

The 361 provenance block has no drift line. The design also says the preflight is "executed unchanged" (line 65), but these checks add to what the contract validates.

The exclusion-based selector admits any non-function, non-class node type. The architecture defines nine file-level types (arch lines 108-110) and is silent on other non-file types. A graph carrying such nodes would hit the drift path in volume.
